================================================================================
SCOPE — what this licence covers, and what it does not
================================================================================

This repository is a mixture of original work and third-party material kept here
so that results are reproducible. The MIT grant above applies ONLY to this
project's own work. Everything listed under "Third-party material" below retains
its own licence and copyright, and nothing here grants any right over it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Covered by the MIT licence above
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  drivers/xtide_mpd/src/     XTIDEMP.ASM and XTIDETR.ASM - this project's
                             Windows 95 SCSI miniport for the Lo-tech XT-CF and
                             XT-IDE cards, and the built XTIDEMP.MPD binary in
                             drivers/xtide_mpd/build/ and dist/xtide_mpd/.
                             Original work, written in MASM. See the note on
                             the Windows 95 DDK below.
  drivers/xtide_pdr/src/     the retired IOS port driver, same terms.
  drivers/*/  *.INF          the INF files written by this project
                             (XTIDEMP.INF, T130-XT.INF, PORT.INF).
  tools/                     the analysis, build and harness scripts.
  vxd-patches/*.py           the patch scripts. See the note on patched
                             Microsoft binaries below.
  ivt68fix/                  IVT68FIX.ASM and the assembled .COM.
  custom_vkd/                the build scripts and this project's changes.
  docs/                      the write-ups, plans and measurements.
  hardware/                  the reverse-engineering notes.
  86box_full/, 86box_upstream/
                             this project's own modifications to 86Box are
                             offered under 86Box's GPL-2.0, not under MIT -
                             they are derivative of it. See below.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party material — each keeps its own licence
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  86box_full/, 86box_upstream/
        86Box, GPL-2.0. See 86box_full/COPYING. This project's changes to 86Box
        are likewise GPL-2.0. Several are merged upstream (86Box PRs #7626,
        #7749, #7761, #7765, #7771).

  drivers/trantor_t130b/T130.MPD, T130.INF, T130.EXE
        Adaptec / Trantor. Redistributed unmodified as a freely downloadable
        driver. Copyright remains with Adaptec.

  drivers/imation_ls120/
        Imation / Shuttle Technology SD120PPD. Copyright remains with Imation.

  drivers/xtide_cdrom/
        OBattler's XT-IDE CD-ROM driver. See that directory's own notes.

  references/cfu1_win9x/
        zikolas/cfu1-win9x, MIT. See references/cfu1_win9x/LICENSE.

  references/3c509b_qemu/, references/ds1315_rtc/
        third-party reference sources; see each directory's own terms.

  roms/
        BIOS images, option ROMs and card ROM dumps. Copyright remains with
        their respective owners (IBM, ATI, Adaptec, and others). Included for
        hardware-fidelity research and reproduction of the results here.

  Patched Microsoft binaries
        Files such as VDMAD.VXD, VPICD.VXD, VKD.VXD, KEYBOARD.DRV, HSFLOP.PDR,
        MSSBLST.VXD and INBRDPC.SYS are Microsoft's (INBRDPC.SYS is Intel's),
        modified here. The MODIFICATIONS, the patch scripts that produce them
        and the analysis describing them are this project's work under MIT; the
        underlying binaries are NOT, and are not licensed by this repository.
        They are included so the fixes can be reproduced and verified.

  Windows 95 DDK
        XTIDEMP.MPD is assembled against Microsoft's 1995 Windows 95 DDK headers
        (SRB.INC, SCSIPORT.INC, MINIPORT.INC) and links SCSIPORT.LIB, as any
        driver built with that DDK does. The DDK itself is not redistributed
        here. The driver source contains no DDK sample code: the sample-derived
        IOS glue belonged to the retired port driver and was removed in the
        rewrite to a miniport.

  Windows 95 itself
        Not included. You need your own OSR1 media.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
If in doubt
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Each driver directory carries a README stating provenance, md5s and, where
applicable, where the file was downloaded from. Those READMEs are the specific
record; this file is the summary. If something here is redistributed in a way
you believe it should not be, please open an issue and it will be removed.
